# Optional avatar preparation (/avatars/prepare on this node): mmpose/mmdet/mmcv stack.
# Group: --with-avatar-prep. cu121 matrix only.
#
# NOT installed with a single `pip install -r`: scripts/install_musetalk.sh installs these in order
# (the same logic scripts/setup_trt_experiment_env.sh used) and uses this file as the list of
# top-level names that `--check` verifies:
#   1. setuptools<81, ninja, psutil               (pip, -c constraints-cu121.txt)
#   2. mmcv==2.1.0 from third_party_wheels/mmcv/  (pip --no-deps); else `mim install mmcv==2.1.0` (openmim is
#      installed --no-deps for that fallback only); else a local wheel build (needs nvcc matching torch's CUDA)
#   3. chumpy==0.70 with --no-build-isolation    (its setup.py imports numpy/pip)
#   4. mmengine, mmdet, mmpose                    (pip, -c constraints-cu121.txt)
# openmim is not required: its opendatalab -> openxlab chain needs rich~=13.4.2, which cannot coexist with
# Kokoro's rich>=13.8 (constraints pin rich 15), so installing it with its dependencies fails to resolve.
setuptools<81
ninja
psutil
mmcv==2.1.0
chumpy
mmengine
mmdet
mmpose
